This project uses github.com/bodgit/sevenzip as a behavioral and architectural
reference. The pinned reference is commit
dcfc72a0ee9f527c55521f44ffdf1c31b732e256, licensed under BSD-3-Clause:

Copyright (c) 2020, Matt Dainty

Phase 2 variable-integer, signature/start-header, serialized header grammar,
file/substream mapping, and selected decoder-property behavior adapted from the
pinned reference are identified precisely in PROVENANCE.md and retain the
upstream BSD-3-Clause notice reproduced in
LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-bodgit-sevenzip.txt.

The Phase 3 Delta, BCJ, BCJ2, PPC, ARM, ARM64, and SPARC decoder work adapts
the pinned reference implementation and retains that notice. The safe Rust
LZMA and LZMA2 decoder adapts github.com/ulikunitz/xz v0.5.15 at commit
7eee8a8a405163554a9accec7b9402ee21400769, Copyright (c) 2014-2022 Ulrich
Kunitz, BSD-3-Clause. Its exact notice is reproduced in
LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-ulikunitz-xz.txt. Exact files, hashes, symbols, and the nature
of each adaptation are recorded in PROVENANCE.md.

The safe Rust PPMd7 variant-H decoder adapts github.com/stangelandcl/ppmd
v0.1.1 at commit e7008704a75379d49824363eca5d87e947b2d9fa,
Copyright (c) 2022 Clayton Stangeland and Copyright (c) 2014 Adam Hathcock,
MIT. Its exact notice is reproduced in LICENSES/MIT-stangelandcl-ppmd.txt. Exact
files, hashes, and adaptation details are recorded in PROVENANCE.md.

The safe Rust ZIP PPMd-I revision-1 decoder adapts Dmitry Shkarin's original
PPMII variant-I sources (written and distributed to the public domain,
1997 and 1999-2002) and Dmitry Subbotin's public-domain carryless range coder
(1999). The canonical source archive, exact mirror revision and file hashes,
excluded mirror-specific additions, and safe-Rust adaptation scope are
recorded in PROVENANCE.md. No PPMd source derived from 7-Zip, p7zip, or an SDK
is used. Packed-layout and control-flow behavior was cross-checked against
SharpCompress's managed I1 port by Michael Bone at commit
e04d51176c5d87668c4c8779825342230c33aa74, Copyright (c) 2014 Adam
Hathcock, MIT; its notice is reproduced in LICENSES/MIT-SharpCompress.txt.

ZIP method 97 decoding uses a decoder-only local fork of `wavicle` 0.1.0 at
commit 4ac1134efe7a85a0b8c5921afc7c124160d179f2, Copyright (c) 2026 Mark,
under its MIT option. The fork omits the encoder and carries recorded
decoder-only, Rust 1.85, checked hostile-input, and fallible-allocation
patches. Its exact MIT notice is reproduced in LICENSES/MIT-wavicle.txt. The
admitted modules identify portions derived from
WavPack 5.9.0 at commit 5803634a030e2a11dba602ba057b89cc34486c67,
Copyright (c) 1998-2025 David Bryant, BSD-3-Clause. The complete upstream
WavPack notice is reproduced in LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-wavpack.txt; exact files,
hashes, and the bounded unpackio adapter are recorded in PROVENANCE.md.

ZIP method 96 decoding adapts the WinZip JPEG metadata parser, arithmetic
model, corrected prediction formulas, and lookup tables from XArchive at commit
c17ca22a2ae75f1d6f97d0a56725655c49b97295, Copyright (c) 2019-2026
hors<horsicq@gmail.com>, MIT. The safe Rust rewrite adds exact outer-stream
accounting, checked arithmetic and allocation, complete table validation,
aggregate resource limits, work accounting, and cancellation. The exact MIT
notice is reproduced in LICENSES/MIT-xarchive.txt; exact source files, hashes,
and adaptation scope are recorded in PROVENANCE.md.

No AES or SHA-256 algorithm implementation is handwritten. Runtime AES-256-CBC
and SHA-256 are supplied by the RustCrypto `aes`, `cbc`, `cipher`, and `sha2`
crates. Deflate, BZip2, Brotli, LZ4, and Zstandard decoding is supplied by the
permissively licensed crates recorded in DEPENDENCIES.md and PROVENANCE.md.

